Check the service catalog before the RBAC Policies panel asks Neutron

RBACPolicies.allowed() in
openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/panel.py returns the
enable_rbac_policy setting and neutron.is_extension_supported(request,
extension_alias='rbac-policies'). The probe reaches networkclient, whose
get_auth_params_from_request calls base.url_for(request, 'network'), and
url_for raises ServiceCatalogException ("Invalid service catalog:
network") when the token's catalog has no network service. The panel's
except Exception then logs "Call to list enabled services failed. This
is likely due to a problem communicating with the Neutron endpoint.
RBAC Policies panel will not be displayed." at ERROR. horizon_nav in
horizon/templatetags/horizon.py calls can_access() of every panel on
every page that renders the sidebar, so a deployment without Neutron
logs the line once per page. The sidebar drops the panel anyway:
horizon/templates/horizon/_sidebar.html filters the panels with
has_permissions_on_list, and the panel declares permissions =
('openstack.services.network',). On a CobaltCore OpenStack ControlPlane
without Neutron (issue #1706), 720 logins an hour produced about 2,160
of these lines an hour, 13,000 of the 33,000 error lines in the
cluster's log store over six hours.

allowed() now checks request.user.has_perms(self.permissions) between
the setting and the probe. has_perms reads the catalog stored with the
session (KeystoneBackend.get_all_permissions in
openstack_auth/backend.py) and makes no network call. It is the
predicate the sidebar applies afterwards, so no user sees a different
sidebar. The six other panels that log the same message (admin and
project trunks, network_qos, volume_groups, vg_snapshots,
server_groups) and the project floating_ip_portforwardings panel check
has_perms before their probe already. A Neutron that is in the catalog
and does not answer still logs the line. The patch does not add
super().allowed(context), which the admin Trunks panel calls, because
the sidebar would then enforce the panel's policy_rules. The patch
needs no operator configuration.

No upstream test calls RBACPolicies.allowed():
openstack_dashboard/test/settings.py mocks RBACPolicies.can_access for
every view test, and the five tests of RBACPolicyTests pass unchanged.
The patch adds RBACPoliciesPanelTests to
openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/tests.py. Its four
tests call allowed() for an active admin user with a valid token, mock
is_extension_supported and watch the panel's LOG.error.
test_allowed_without_network_service_skips_the_probe gives a catalog
without a network service and an empty one, and its probe mock raises
ServiceCatalogException the way url_for does: False, no probe, no log
line. test_allowed_with_network_service_asks_neutron returns the
probe's answer. test_allowed_logs_when_the_probe_fails raises
ConnectFailure from the probe: False and one log line.
test_allowed_with_the_setting_off_skips_the_probe turns
enable_rbac_policy off and skips the probe, and a missing key falls back
to the default True. Without the panel.py hunk
test_allowed_without_network_service_skips_the_probe fails, because
the probe runs and the panel logs the line.

Proof: test_rbac_policies_panel_checks_catalog_first in
tests/container-images/verify_horizon.sh calls allowed() in the built
image with a catalog without a network service and asserts False and no
ERROR record, then with a network service and a mocked probe and
asserts True and one probe call.

The 2026.1 twin carries the same hunks: panel.py and tests.py are
identical in 25.7.0 and 27.0.0.

Applies to horizon 27.0.0 (2026.2).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

diff --git a/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/panel.py b/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/panel.py
index b3198db..4b24bc6 100644
--- a/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/panel.py
+++ b/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/panel.py
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ class RBACPolicies(horizon.Panel):
             return (
                 setting_utils.get_dict_config(
                     'OPENSTACK_NEUTRON_NETWORK', 'enable_rbac_policy') and
+                request.user.has_perms(self.permissions) and
                 neutron.is_extension_supported(request,
                                                extension_alias='rbac-policies')
             )
diff --git a/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/tests.py b/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/tests.py
index 226e91b..cef3ffc 100644
--- a/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/tests.py
+++ b/openstack_dashboard/dashboards/admin/rbac_policies/tests.py
@@ -14,9 +14,16 @@
 
 from unittest import mock
 
+from django.conf import settings
+from django.test.utils import override_settings
 from django.urls import reverse
+from keystoneauth1 import exceptions as ks_exceptions
+from openstack_auth import user as auth_user
+
+from horizon import exceptions as horizon_exceptions
 
 from openstack_dashboard import api
+from openstack_dashboard.dashboards.admin.rbac_policies import panel
 from openstack_dashboard.test import helpers as test
 
 INDEX_TEMPLATE = 'horizon/common/_data_table_view.html'
@@ -181,3 +188,83 @@ class RBACPolicyTests(test.BaseAdminViewTests):
         self.assert_mock_multiple_calls_with_same_arguments(
             self.mock_is_extension_supported, 2,
             mock.call(test.IsHttpRequest(), extension_alias='qos'))
+
+
+class RBACPoliciesPanelTests(test.BaseAdminViewTests):
+    """RBACPolicies.allowed() asks Neutron only for a network service."""
+
+    def _allowed(self, service_catalog):
+        request = self.factory.get('/')
+        request.user = auth_user.User(
+            id=self.user.id, token=self.token, user=self.user.name,
+            tenant_id=self.tenant.id, service_catalog=service_catalog,
+            roles=[self.roles.admin._info], services_region='RegionOne',
+            enabled=True, endpoint=settings.OPENSTACK_KEYSTONE_URL)
+        # An inactive user, or one without a valid token, holds no
+        # service permission whatever its catalog says, and the tests
+        # below would then pass for the wrong reason.
+        self.assertTrue(request.user.is_authenticated)
+        self.assertTrue(request.user.is_active)
+        return panel.RBACPolicies().allowed({'request': request})
+
+    @test.create_mocks({api.neutron: ('is_extension_supported',)})
+    def test_allowed_without_network_service_skips_the_probe(self):
+        # Without a network service, url_for in the real probe raises.
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.side_effect = (
+            horizon_exceptions.ServiceCatalogException('network'))
+        catalogs = {
+            'without network': [service for service in self.service_catalog
+                                if service['type'] != 'network'],
+            'empty': [],
+        }
+        for name, catalog in catalogs.items():
+            with self.subTest(catalog=name), \
+                    mock.patch.object(panel.LOG, 'error') as mock_error:
+                self.assertFalse(self._allowed(catalog))
+                mock_error.assert_not_called()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.assert_not_called()
+
+    @test.create_mocks({api.neutron: ('is_extension_supported',)})
+    def test_allowed_with_network_service_asks_neutron(self):
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.return_value = True
+        with mock.patch.object(panel.LOG, 'error') as mock_error:
+            self.assertTrue(self._allowed(self.service_catalog))
+        mock_error.assert_not_called()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.assert_called_once_with(
+            test.IsHttpRequest(), extension_alias='rbac-policies')
+
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.reset_mock()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.return_value = False
+        with mock.patch.object(panel.LOG, 'error') as mock_error:
+            self.assertFalse(self._allowed(self.service_catalog))
+        mock_error.assert_not_called()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.assert_called_once_with(
+            test.IsHttpRequest(), extension_alias='rbac-policies')
+
+    @test.create_mocks({api.neutron: ('is_extension_supported',)})
+    def test_allowed_logs_when_the_probe_fails(self):
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.side_effect = (
+            ks_exceptions.ConnectFailure('Unable to establish connection'))
+        with mock.patch.object(panel.LOG, 'error') as mock_error:
+            self.assertFalse(self._allowed(self.service_catalog))
+        mock_error.assert_called_once()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.assert_called_once_with(
+            test.IsHttpRequest(), extension_alias='rbac-policies')
+
+    @test.create_mocks({api.neutron: ('is_extension_supported',)})
+    def test_allowed_with_the_setting_off_skips_the_probe(self):
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.return_value = True
+        with override_settings(
+                OPENSTACK_NEUTRON_NETWORK={'enable_rbac_policy': False}), \
+                mock.patch.object(panel.LOG, 'error') as mock_error:
+            self.assertFalse(self._allowed(self.service_catalog))
+        mock_error.assert_not_called()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.assert_not_called()
+
+        # Without the key, get_dict_config falls back to the default True.
+        with override_settings(OPENSTACK_NEUTRON_NETWORK={}), \
+                mock.patch.object(panel.LOG, 'error') as mock_error:
+            self.assertTrue(self._allowed(self.service_catalog))
+        mock_error.assert_not_called()
+        self.mock_is_extension_supported.assert_called_once_with(
+            test.IsHttpRequest(), extension_alias='rbac-policies')
